 ["Which sensory receptor detects muscle stretch and contributes to stretch reflex?","Muscle stretch पत्ता लगाई stretch reflex मा योगदान गर्ने receptor कुन हो?",["Muscle spindle","Golgi tendon organ only","Photoreceptor","Chemoreceptor"],0,"Muscle spindles detect muscle length and rate of stretch and contribute to stretch reflexes.","Muscle spindle ले muscle length र stretch rate पत्ता लगाउँछ।","Section 1"],
 ["Which receptor responds to tension in a tendon?","Tendon मा tension पत्ता लगाउने receptor कुन हो?",["Golgi tendon organ","Muscle spindle","Rods and cones","Pacinian corpuscle only"],0,"Golgi tendon organs respond to muscle-tendon tension and contribute to force regulation.","Golgi tendon organ ले muscle-tendon tension पत्ता लगाउँछ।","Section 1"],
 ["Which energy system predominates during very brief maximal effort?","अति छोटो maximal effort मा कुन energy system प्रमुख हुन्छ?",["ATP-phosphocreatine system","Aerobic fat oxidation only","Protein breakdown only","Lactic acid storage system"],0,"The ATP-phosphocreatine system supplies rapid energy for brief, high-intensity efforts.","ATP-phosphocreatine system ले छोटो, उच्च तीव्रताको प्रयासमा छिटो energy दिन्छ।","Section 1"],
 ["What is the primary purpose of a goniometer?","Goniometer को मुख्य प्रयोग के हो?",["Measure joint range of motion","Measure blood glucose","Measure lung volume","Measure body temperature"],0,"A goniometer measures joint angles and helps document range of motion.","Goniometer ले joint angle र ROM मापन गर्छ।","Section 2"],
 ["Which test commonly assesses functional balance and fall risk?","Functional balance र fall risk मूल्याङ्कन गर्न कुन test प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Berg Balance Scale","Snellen chart","Widal test","Apgar score"],0,"The Berg Balance Scale evaluates functional balance tasks and can help assess fall risk.","Berg Balance Scale ले functional balance जाँचेर fall risk मूल्याङ्कनमा सहयोग गर्छ।","Section 2"],
 ["Which test measures functional exercise capacity by distance walked in six minutes?","छ मिनेटमा हिँडेको दूरीबाट functional exercise capacity मापन गर्ने test कुन हो?",["Six-Minute Walk Test","Timed Up and Go only","Romberg test","MMT"],0,"The Six-Minute Walk Test records distance walked in six minutes under a standardized protocol.","Six-Minute Walk Test मा standard protocol अनुसार 6 मिनेटमा हिँडेको दूरी नापिन्छ।","Section 2"],
 ["What is the main purpose of a walking aid?","Walking aid को मुख्य उद्देश्य के हो?",["Improve safety and support during mobility","Replace all exercise permanently","Guarantee that falls cannot occur","Increase pain intentionally"],0,"A correctly selected and fitted aid can improve support, balance and mobility safety.","सही aid ले support, balance र mobility safety सुधार्न सक्छ।","Section 2"],
 ["Before gait training with a patient after surgery, what should be checked first?","Surgery पछि gait training अघि पहिले के जाँच्नुपर्छ?",["Medical stability and weight-bearing instructions","Only shoe colour","Only room temperature","Ignore surgical precautions"],0,"Check medical stability, surgical precautions, weight-bearing status, pain and assistance needs.","Medical stability, surgical precaution, weight-bearing, pain र सहयोगको आवश्यकता जाँच्नुहोस्।","Section 2"],
 ["Which exercise type is performed by the patient without external assistance?","बिरामीले बाह्य सहयोग बिना गर्ने exercise कुन हो?",["Active exercise","Passive exercise","Assisted exercise","Machine-only movement"],0,"Active exercise is produced by the patient's own muscle contraction.","Active exercise बिरामीको आफ्नै muscle contraction बाट हुन्छ।","Section 2"],
 ["Which exercise is performed by an external force while the patient remains relaxed?","बिरामी relaxed हुँदा बाह्य बलबाट गरिने exercise कुन हो?",["Passive range of motion","Active strengthening","Resisted exercise","Aerobic interval training"],0,"Passive ROM is moved by an external force without voluntary muscle effort from the patient.","Passive ROM बाह्य बलले गरिन्छ, बिरामीले voluntary muscle effort गर्दैन।","Section 2"],
 ["Which principle means gradually increasing exercise demand as capacity improves?","क्षमता बढ्दै जाँदा exercise demand क्रमशः बढाउने principle कुन हो?",["Progressive overload","Immobilization","Avoidance","Random loading"],0,"Progressive overload increases training demand gradually and appropriately to stimulate adaptation.","Progressive overload ले adaptation का लागि training demand क्रमशः बढाउँछ।","Section 2"],
 ["Which parameter should be monitored during aerobic exercise in a medically vulnerable patient?","Medical risk भएको बिरामीमा aerobic exercise गर्दा कुन parameter monitor गर्नुपर्छ?",["Symptoms, heart rate, blood pressure and oxygen saturation as indicated","Hair length","Hand dominance only","Room decoration"],0,"Monitoring is individualized to diagnosis and risk and may include symptoms, HR, BP and SpO2.","Diagnosis र risk अनुसार symptoms, HR, BP र SpO2 monitor गर्न सकिन्छ।","Section 2"],
 ["What is the main aim of a home exercise programme?","Home exercise programme को मुख्य लक्ष्य के हो?",["Support safe, regular practice toward agreed functional goals","Replace all follow-up care","Use the same plan for every patient","Exercise through severe warning symptoms"],0,"A home programme should be individualized, understandable, safe and linked to functional goals.","Home programme व्यक्तिगत, बुझ्न सजिलो, सुरक्षित र functional goal सँग सम्बन्धित हुनुपर्छ।","Section 2"]
